            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0514" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg378"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">580.7A3/420: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-29T20:00:00-04:00">May 29, 1929—8
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>131. For White. Your 131, May 28, noon. Department considers that in order to
                    avoid possible misunderstanding and the necessity for making explanations you
                    should follow instructions March 28 concerning reservation.</p>
                <p>This Government has not signed the Counterfeiting Convention.<anchor n="9a"
                        xml:id="d222-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
